0 -14 Td
(A horizontal seam is a vertical seam in a transposed image. The carver transposes the energy) Tj
0 -14 Td
(map, calls the same DP function, and converts the result back. This is why one DP) Tj
0 -14 Td
(implementation correctly handles both vertical and horizontal resizing.) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -10 Td
(For each seam, carve\(\) performs this sequence:) Tj
0 -14 Td
(1. Compute a fresh energy map for the current image.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(2. Call find_vertical_seam_dp\(\) on the energy map.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(3. Validate the seam and remove one selected pixel per row.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(4. Repeat until the requested width and height are reached.) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -10 Td
(The energy map is recomputed after every removal because the removed seam changes the) Tj
0 -14 Td
(neighbouring pixels and therefore their energy. This directly satisfies Q1\(a\), Q1\(b\), and) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Q1\(c\).) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -10 Td
(Complexity) Tj
0 -14 Td
